## Decisions locked this session

- **The conversation IS the request** (author ruling). No separate ticket-raising step. A turn
  carries an intent: `clarify` (answer, nothing changes) or `edit` (may produce a proposal).
- **Push back is a first-class outcome.** An edit request may return a reasoned refusal
  ("this plants the payoff in Ch30") instead of a proposal. Refusing is a position, not a veto.
- **Confirmation before acting on a request.** Restate what was heard + the steps, then wait. With
  voice this is the *only* error correction — a misheard word otherwise edits the wrong sentence.
  **Questions must never confirm** (confirmation fatigue).
- **Intent is inferred, not chosen.** The Clarify/Edit toggle becomes an override; default `auto`.
- **Seamless means free and fast.** Anything metered gets rationed. Local TTS (Piper) preferred;
  ElevenLabs only for the deliberate "book voice". STT via **Groq `whisper-large-v3-turbo`**
  (vault key exists, lowest latency) — not whisper.cpp.
- **Transport is `IToolCallingLlm`, not `ILlmService`.** That one swap gives BYOK, key-pool
  failover, Claude→OpenAI fallback, multi-turn, and tool calls.
- **Claude has NO fallback below a BYO key** (2026-08-25 author ruling). Do not "fix" this. The UI
  shows a no-key state and links to Settings; nothing is spent.
- **Anchors resolve against reader-visible text**, not stored markup — entity-tag re-derivation
  churns stored text ~55 chars per wrapper without moving what a reader sees.
- **All UI lives in Prose.WriterUi compiled into Hub.exe.** Writer.exe is a WebView2 frame. No new
  apps (Prose.Codex / Prose.Atlas were considered and dropped).
- Blocks are typed + `[JsonDerivedType]`; `TargetKind`/block `type` are **strings**, so a new
  surface costs no migration.

